  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "No matter what security settings you have, a freshly created account can come into your world and crash the whole instance by spamming invalid RPCs, even when you block them, forcing you to restart VRChat (since everything stops working and slowly falls apart).\nThe situation is even worse because VRChat doesn't log where those RPCs are coming from, so I can't investigate it and report the user or kick them from the world. However, it should be easy for VRChat to detect if someone is spamming those Emoji RPCs in an unusual amount and auto-disconnect the user before damage is done. \nExample:\n2021.04.17 15:37:18 Error      -  [Behaviour] Could not find target for [SendRPC/AlwaysUnbuffered w: 3814 s: SpawnEmojiRPC i: 0 f: 0 b: 255 B: 8 p: :16BBB3C1/]",
  "error": null,
